  "description": "Opened as its own run rather than continuing run/0018, deliberately and at a cost. item/ledger-mutation-nodes shipped last hour with MUTATION_RULES_EFFECTIVE_AFTER_RUN = 18, so rule 1 -- a Completed spec:10 item must be implements-referenced by a negative Mutation with a non-empty check -- binds from run/0019 onward and grandfathers everything at or below 18. item/home-dashboard is spec:10. Keeping it on run/0018 would have exempted it from the rule this loop shipped an hour earlier, which is gaming its own guard: the run boundary is not a place to buy an exemption. So this run starts here and the rule binds, and item/home-dashboard cannot be recorded Completed without a mutation node that names the assertion shown to fail. run/0018 closes green: main verified at 221b30e across all ten jobs from main's own push run, after decision/0039's fix to the smoke's upload gate. Its tests/assertions read -1, not 701/1446. The 701/1446 this file carried were run/0018's, copied forward when the run was opened and never re-measured -- while this run merged three items, each adding tests. A copied number reads as a measurement, so it is worse than no number. It cannot be re-measured here (there is no vendor/ in this environment, so the suite runs only in CI), and -1 is what the schema already permits for a value that was not taken. item/ledger-field-audit decides whether -1 gains that meaning formally or the two fields are removed; run/0016 and run/0017 carry the same defect, byte-identical at 649/1340 across a run that merged three items."
